[
 "Every GPS satellite", "is launched", "with its clock", "set wrong.", "On purpose.",
 "Your phone finds you", "by timing", "radio signals", "from satellites", "twenty thousand", "kilometres up.",
 "Light covers", "thirty centimetres", "in a billionth", "of a second.",
 "So a clock", "that's a billionth off", "puts you", "thirty centimetres off.",
 "But Einstein showed", "that time doesn't tick", "at the same rate", "everywhere.",
 "Up there,", "gravity is weaker,", "so the clock", "runs fast,", "by about forty-five", "microseconds a day.",
 "It's also moving", "at almost", "four kilometres", "a second,", "which slows it down", "by about seven.",
 "Net result:", "thirty-eight", "microseconds fast.", "Every single day.",
 "That sounds", "like nothing.", "But at the speed", "of light,", "it's more than", "eleven kilometres.",
 "Ignore it,", "and your blue dot", "drifts that far off", "in a single day.",
 "In 1977,", "not everyone", "believed it.",
 "So the Navy's", "test satellite,", "NTS-2,", "flew with the fix", "built in,", "but switched off.",
 "They'd only", "turn it on", "if Einstein", "turned out to be right.",
 "For about", "twenty days,", "the clock ran", "uncorrected.",
 "Einstein's math", "predicted", "how fast it would run.",
 "The clock", "matched him", "to within", "one percent.",
 "They flipped", "the switch.",
 "Ever since,", "every GPS clock", "is tuned", "a hair slow", "before launch.",
 "Wrong on the ground,", "so it's right", "in the sky.",
 "And every time", "that blue dot", "finds you,", "Einstein passes", "the test again."
